{"id":"n4-095","title":"～てはいけない (〜te wa ikenai)","jlptLevel":4,"shortExplanation":"Expresses prohibition; 'must not', 'cannot'.","longExplanation":"The ～てはいけない grammar point is used to express strict prohibition or something that must not be done. It can be translated as 'must not', 'cannot', or 'should not' in English. It is formed by adding て-form of a verb followed by はいけない.","formation":"Verb-て-form + はいけない","examples":[{"jp":"公園でたばこを吸ってはいけない。","romaji":"Kouen de tabako o sutte wa ikenai.","en":"You must not smoke in the park.","words":[{"surface":"公園","vocabId":"1273270","reading":"こうえん"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"たばこ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"吸っ","vocabId":"1228260","reading":"すう"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いけ","vocabId":"1421700","reading":"いけ"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"ここで写真を撮ってはいけない。","romaji":"Koko de shashin o totte wa ikenai.","en":"You cannot take pictures here.","words":[{"surface":"ここ","vocabId":"1288810","reading":"ここ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"写真","vocabId":"1321900","reading":"しゃしん"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"撮っ","vocabId":"1298790","reading":"とる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いけ","vocabId":"1421700","reading":"いけ"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"図書館で大きな声を出してはいけない。","romaji":"Toshokan de ookina koe o dashite wa ikenai.","en":"You must not speak loudly in the library.","words":[{"surface":"図書館","vocabId":"1370420","reading":"としょかん"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"大きな","vocabId":null},{"surface":"声","vocabId":"1380440","reading":"こえ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"出し","vocabId":"1339160","reading":"だし"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いけ","vocabId":"1421700","reading":"いけ"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","v